\newlabel{fig_intro_div-19}{{6}{6}{A sample image from Flower dataset before (top) and after (bottom) the top-$k$ attributional attack of \citet  {ghorbani2018interpretation} on a ResNet model. For both, we show from left to right: the image, its top-$k$ diverse pixels as per IG, the union of $3 \times 3$-pixel neighborhoods and $5 \times 5$-pixel neighborhoods of the top-$k$ diverse pixels, respectively, for $k=1000$. Quantitatively, improved overlap is captured by top-$k$-div intersection: 0.22, $1$-LENS-recall@$k$-div: 0.87, $1$-LENS-pre@$k$-div: 0.86, $2$-LENS-recall@$k$-div: 0.95, $2$-LENS-pre@$k$-div: 0.93. \emph  {Zoom in required to see the diverse pixels.}}{}{}}
